{% extends 'TechBundle::layout.twig' %}
{% block content %}

<div class="block"><div class="content">
	<h2>Introduction to Usersources</h2>
	<div class="inner">
		<p>
			Usersources allow you to configure remote resources that feed your helpdesk authentication information.
			This allows you to let your users log in using credentials from other systems such as your website, or even popular
			social networks like Twitter or Facebook.
		</p>

		<p>
			Usersources are also used to fetch user information to make it easy to keep your users contact information up to date
			and complete. You can configure your helpdesk to sync from systems like Highrise.
		</p>

		<p>
			If you have your own systems, you can implement your own integrations by implementing a set of simple protocols.
			Refer to the <a href="">help pages</a> for information and examples.
		</p>
	</div>
</div></div>

{% if has_no_usersources %}
	<div class="block"><div class="content">
		<h2>Create a Usersource</h2>
		<div class="inner">
			<p>
				You currently have no usersources defined. This means all users will only be able to register and log in using the helpdesk.
				We recommend creating new sources for popular websites such as Twitter and Facebook to increase the ease in which
				users can gain access to your helpdesk.
			</p>
			<form action="{% path 'tech_admin_usersources_new' %}" method="get">
				<div class="group navform wat-cf">
					<button class="button" type="submit">
						<img src="{% asset 'images/icons/tick.png' %}" alt="Save" /> Create a new usersource
					</button>
				</div>
			</form>
		</div>
	</div></div>
{% endif %}


{% endblock %}
{% block sidebar %}
	<div class="block notice">
		<h4>Need Help?</h4>
		<p>
			Read the <a href="">help pages</a> regarding usersources for more information.
		</p>
	</div>
{% endblock %}